  "id": "EDU056",
  "title": "The Reversible Door",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "work/process",
  "premise": "A product team wants to test two layouts, but treats a replaceable mockup as if it were a permanent public launch. Marking reversibility and consequence lets them try the mockup while reserving review for the lasting decision.",
  "hook": "Which door lets us walk back out?",
  "visible_action": "Two doors display undo paths; a sandbox preview loops back while a public-release door requires a review key.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Decision process should reflect consequences, reversibility, and actual authority.",
  "gate": "Reversibility never substitutes for required permission, privacy, or safety review.",
